meta {
  name: Zerodha Publisher
  seq: 10
}

docs {
  Zerodha Kite Publisher flow — lets users submit orders via Kite's hosted basket confirmation
  page instead of direct API (no algo-trading risk framework needed for retail users).

  **Prerequisite:** Zerodha live credential with `execution_mode: "publisher"` (single API key,
  no access token needed). See Credentials → create-zerodha-publisher.

  **Flow:**
  1. POST signal to webhook → worker creates publisher_order (status=`created`)
     → trade status set to `pending_confirmation`, `broker_order` = publisher order UUID.
  2. GET /v1/publisher/orders/:id — fetch handoff form fields (api_key + basket data JSON).
  3. Dashboard POSTs hidden form to https://kite.zerodha.com/connect/basket — user sees basket.
  4. User confirms → Kite redirects to GET /v1/publisher/callback?status=success&state=<signed>
     User cancels  → Kite redirects to GET /v1/publisher/callback?status=cancelled&state=<signed>
  5. Backend validates HMAC state, updates publisher_order + trade, redirects to frontend.
  6. GET /v1/trades/:id — check final trade status (submitted / pending_confirmation).

  **Publisher order statuses:** created → awaiting_confirmation → user_returned | user_cancelled | expired
  **Trade statuses:**          pending_confirmation → submitted (on user_returned + settlement)

  **State token:** HMAC-SHA256 signed, 30-minute expiry, URL-safe base64.
  Format: base64RawURL(publisherOrderID | expiresUnix | hmac)

  See: docs/broker-guide.md → Kite Publisher section.
}
